   "text": "You are comparing two drafts written from the same brief. Read no other file, and do not run commands or browse; judge only the text below.\n\nBrief: Write the README's opening paragraph and its Install and update section for the `tidy-hooks` plugin.\n\n<<<DRAFT A\n`tidy-hooks` is a Claude and Codex plugin that blocks `git commit` when staged files contain merge markers.\n\n## Install and update\n\n### Claude\n\nAdd the marketplace, then install the plugin:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin marketplace add example/tidy\nclaude plugin install tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\nTo update:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin update tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\n### Codex\n\nAdd the marketplace, then install the plugin:\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace add example/tidy\ncodex plugin add tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\nReview and trust the plugin hooks. Codex skips them until you do.\n\nTo update, run:\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace upgrade tidy\n```\n\nThen restart Codex.\n\nIf Node.js is missing, commits proceed without the hook blocking them.\nDRAFT A>>>\n\n<<<DRAFT B\n`tidy-hooks` is a Claude and Codex plugin that blocks `git commit` when staged files contain merge markers. If Node.js is missing, commits proceed.\n\n## Install and update\n\n### Claude\n\nInstall:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin marketplace add example/tidy\nclaude plugin install tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\nUpdate:\n\n```sh\nclaude plugin update tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\n### Codex\n\nInstall:\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace add example/tidy\ncodex plugin add tidy-hooks@tidy\n```\n\nReview and trust the plugin hooks. Codex skips them until you do.\n\nUpdate:\n\n```sh\ncodex plugin marketplace upgrade tidy\n```\n\nThen restart Codex.\nDRAFT B>>>\n\nAnswer each question with \"A\", \"B\", or \"SAME\":\n- \"reader\": Could a first-time reader do what they came to do?\n- \"careful\": Does it read like a careful person wrote it?\n- \"overall\": Which draft is better overall?\n\nReply with only JSON: {\"reader\": \"A\", \"careful\": \"A\", \"overa